om2
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note bridge/shlib/shlib.om: writes an AArch64 Linux shared library (ELF64 ET_DYN) from a table and the native
note object omc emits for an OM-2 unit with `export fn` entries, and a probe executable that loads it through the
note system's dynamic loader and calls it. No C compiler, assembler or linker is involved.
note Build: seed/out/omc < bridge/shlib/shlib.om > shlib
note   shlib lib TABLE OBJECT OUT   the library: DT_SONAME from TABLE, one global function symbol per export row
note   shlib call TABLE OUT         the probe: an executable that needs the TABLE's SONAME (searched next to the
note                                probe, DT_RUNPATH $ORIGIN, bound at load), makes each call row's call in order
note                                and exits 0 when every result matches, 1+k (200 for k >= 199) when call k does
note                                not, 250 when x19..x27 or the stack pointer did not come back unchanged
note OBJECT is omc's output for the line "object" followed by the unit (OMOBJ001, spec/omegese-modules.md).
note TABLE: one row per line, fields separated by one tab; an empty line or one starting with # is skipped.
note   soname NAME               the library's DT_SONAME (exactly one row)
note   unit PATH                 the unit the object is compiled from (a record for the reader; not read here)
note   export NAME TRAP          NAME, an `export fn` of the object, becomes a global function symbol; a trap
note                             inside it returns TRAP (0..4294967295) to the C caller
note   call NAME EXPECT ARG...   the probe calls NAME with up to 6 arguments (a decimal 64-bit value, or buf for
note                             a pointer to 4096 zeroed writable bytes) and compares the low 32 bits of the
note                             result with EXPECT
note From the C calling convention (AAPCS64) to omc's function ABI, per export: each C argument register is one
note omc parameter slot, in order (a scalar or a sized array: one slot; an unsized view or edit: a pointer slot
note then a ulong count slot). Narrow integer arguments are sign- or zero-extended as omc expects. x7 points at a
note per-call context on the caller's stack whose entry 16 is the trap entry; x19..x30 and d8..d15 are saved
note there and restored on both the return and the trap path. The result is returned in x0.
note Refused (exit 1, nothing written): an object that is not an OMOBJ001 version 1 AArch64 object or has
note trailing bytes, an object with an imported function, code that loads a runtime entry other than the trap
note entry ([x7, #16]), a float parameter or result (omc passes them in x registers, C in v registers), a table
note export that is not an export of the object, a repeated or malformed name, a malformed row or number, no
note soname or no export, a call of a name that is no export of the table.
note Exit 0 written, 1 refused, 2 usage, 3 a file unreadable or unwritable or memory refused.
note Every buffer is a run-time pool sized from its input. The ADR and LDR literal reach (1 MiB) and the B and BL
note reach (128 MiB) of AArch64 are real boundaries: an output past them is refused, never truncated.
global ib uchar *
global eb uchar *
global ds uchar *
global ex ulong *
global cl ulong *
global cd ulong *
global fr ulong *
global ag uchar 4096
global fo ulong 16
global fl ulong 16
global nv ulong 64
global ly ulong 32
note nv: 0 table end (object start), 1 object end, 2 dynstr length, 3 exports, 4 calls, 5 soname offset in ib,
note 6 soname length, 7 functions, 8 code end, 9 fields in the current row, 10 output length, 13 soname in
note dynstr, 14 runpath in dynstr, 15 section header offset, 16 address minus offset of the current section
note ex, per export (8): 0 name offset in ib, 1 name length, 2 trap value, 3 function index, 4 dynstr offset,
note 5 wrapper offset in .text, 6 wrapper bytes, 7 extensions
note cl, per call (16): 0 name offset, 1 name length, 2 expect, 3 arguments, 4..9 values, 10..15 1 for buf
note cd, per call: the dynstr offset of its name
note fr, per object function (8): 0 flags, 1 address, 2 result type, 3 parameters, 4 parameter records offset
note in ib, 5 name offset in ib, 6 name length
text m_lib "lib"
text m_call "call"
text k_son "soname"
text k_unit "unit"
text k_exp "export"
text k_call "call"
text k_buf "buf"
text k_obj "OMOBJ001"
text t_interp "/lib/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1"
text t_origin "$ORIGIN"
note the section names, each space written as a zero
text t_shs " .hash .dynsym .dynstr .text .dynamic .shstrtab "
text e_usage "usage: shlib lib TABLE OBJECT OUT | shlib call TABLE OUT\n"
text e_read "shlib: cannot read an input file\n"
text e_write "shlib: cannot write the output file\n"
text e_mem "shlib: memory refused\n"
text e_row "shlib: malformed table row\n"
text e_num "shlib: malformed number in the table\n"
text e_name "shlib: a name outside A-Z a-z 0-9 _ (1..63 bytes) or repeated\n"
text e_son "shlib: the table needs exactly one soname row\n"
text e_noexp "shlib: the table names no export\n"
text e_trap "shlib: a trap value above 4294967295\n"
text e_obj "shlib: the object is not an OMOBJ001 version 1 AArch64 object\n"
text e_imp "shlib: the object imports a function; imports are not linked here\n"
text e_rt "shlib: the code loads a runtime entry other than the trap entry\n"
text e_miss "shlib: a table export is not an export of the object\n"
text e_flt "shlib: a float parameter or result; refused\n"
text e_slot "shlib: more than 6 parameter slots\n"
text e_ncall "shlib: a call names no export of the table\n"
text e_reach "shlib: output past the AArch64 branch or literal reach\n"
note ---- small helpers
fn die t view uchar * code int to void
r = write 2 t 0 len t
exit code
end
fn al8 x ulong to ulong
ret and add x 7 not ulong 7
end
fn al16 x ulong to ulong
ret and add x 15 not ulong 15
end
fn w8 o ulong v ulong to void
put eb o uchar and v 255
end
fn w16 o ulong v ulong to void
w8 o v
w8 add o 1 shr v 8
end
fn w32 o ulong v ulong to void
w16 o and v 65535
w16 add o 2 shr v 16
end
fn w64 o ulong v ulong to void
w32 o and v 4294967295
w32 add o 4 shr v 32
end
note the u32 of eb at o
fn r32 o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for i ulong 4
v = or v shl ulong get eb add o i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
note the u64 of ib at o, inside the object
fn q o ulong to ulong
if gt add o 8 get nv 1
die e_obj 1
end
v = ulong 0
for i ulong 8
v = or v shl ulong get ib add o i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
note the u64 at object offset o
fn oq o ulong to ulong
ret q add get nv 0 o
end
note argument ai into ag; its length
fn ap ai ulong to ulong
r = argread ai ag 0 4095
if le r 0
die e_usage 2
end
ret ulong r
end
fn argis ai ulong t view uchar * to bool
r = argread ai ag 0 4095
if ne r long len t
ret false
end
for i ulong len t bound 4096
if ne get ag i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note append argument ai's file to ib from offset at; the new end
fn ldf ai ulong from ulong to ulong
m = ap ai
fd = fopen ag 0 m int 524288 int 0
if lt fd 0
die e_read 3
end
n = from
while true bound 9223372036854775807
if lt sub len ib n 65536
r = enlarge ib add add n 65536 len ib
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
end
x = read int fd ib n sub len ib n
if lt x 0
die e_read 3
end
if eq x 0
break
end
n = add n ulong x
end
r = fclose int fd
ret n
end
note write eb[0, nv 10) to argument ai's path with mode md
fn save ai ulong md int to void
m = ap ai
r = unlink ag 0 m
fd = fopen ag 0 m int 524865 md
if lt fd 0
die e_write 3
end
n = get nv 10
o = ulong 0
while lt o n bound 9223372036854775807
x = write int fd eb o sub n o
if le x 0
die e_write 3
end
o = add o ulong x
end
r = fclose int fd
if lt r 0
die e_write 3
end
end
note eb grown to n bytes, all zero
fn ebnew n ulong to void
if gt n len eb
r = enlarge eb n
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
end
for i ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
put eb i 0
end
put nv 10 n
end
note ---- table rows: the fields of one line into fo/fl, their count into nv 9; returns the next line
fn row o ulong e ulong to ulong
put nv 9 0
s = o
p = o
while lt p e bound 9223372036854775807
c = get ib p
if eq c 10
break
end
if eq c 9
k = get nv 9
if ge k 15
die e_row 1
end
put fo k s
put fl k sub p s
put nv 9 add k 1
s = add p 1
end
p = add p 1
end
k = get nv 9
put fo k s
put fl k sub p s
put nv 9 add k 1
if lt p e
p = add p 1
end
ret p
end
fn ft i ulong t view uchar * to bool
if ne get fl i len t
ret false
end
o = get fo i
for j ulong len t bound 4096
if ne get ib add o j get t j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note field i as a decimal u64
fn fnum i ulong to ulong
n = get fl i
if or eq n 0 gt n 20
die e_num 1
end
o = get fo i
v = ulong 0
for j ulong n bound 20
c = get ib add o j
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
die e_num 1
end
d = ulong sub c 48
if gt v div sub 18446744073709551615 d 10
die e_num 1
end
v = add mul v 10 d
end
ret v
end
note ib[a, a+n) equals ib[b, b+n)
fn same a ulong b ulong n ulong to bool
for j ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
if ne get ib add a j get ib add b j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note field i is a name: 1..63 bytes of A-Z a-z 0-9 _, and also . + - when so (a soname)
fn fname i ulong so bool to void
n = get fl i
if or eq n 0 gt n 63
die e_name 1
end
o = get fo i
for j ulong n bound 63
c = get ib add o j
ok = or and ge c 48 le c 57 eq c 95
ok = or ok or and ge c 65 le c 90 and ge c 97 le c 122
if so
ok = or ok or or eq c 46 eq c 43 eq c 45
end
if not ok
die e_name 1
end
end
end
note the export named ib[a, a+n), or the export count when none
fn exfind a ulong n ulong to ulong
nx = get nv 3
for k ulong nx bound 9223372036854775807
b = mul k 8
if eq get ex add b 1 n
if same get ex b a n
ret k
end
end
end
ret nx
end
fn exrow to void
if ne get nv 9 3
die e_row 1
end
fname 1 false
nx = get nv 3
if ne exfind get fo 1 get fl 1 nx
die e_name 1
end
t = fnum 2
if gt t 4294967295
die e_trap 1
end
r = enlarge ex mul add nx 1 8
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
b = mul nx 8
put ex b get fo 1
put ex add b 1 get fl 1
put ex add b 2 t
put nv 3 add nx 1
end
fn callrow to void
nf = get nv 9
if or lt nf 3 gt nf 9
die e_row 1
end
fname 1 false
nc = get nv 4
r = enlarge cl mul add nc 1 16
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
b = mul nc 16
put cl b get fo 1
put cl add b 1 get fl 1
e = fnum 2
if gt e 4294967295
die e_num 1
end
put cl add b 2 e
na = sub nf 3
put cl add b 3 na
for j ulong na bound 6
f = add j 3
if ft f k_buf
put cl add add b 10 j 1
else
put cl add add b 4 j fnum f
end
end
put nv 4 add nc 1
end
fn parse to void
p = ulong 0
e = get nv 0
ns = ulong 0
while lt p e bound 9223372036854775807
p = row p e
skip = and eq get nv 9 1 eq get fl 0 0
if gt get fl 0 0
if eq get ib get fo 0 35
skip = true
end
end
if not skip
if ft 0 k_son
if ne get nv 9 2
die e_row 1
end
fname 1 true
put nv 5 get fo 1
put nv 6 get fl 1
ns = add ns 1
else
if ft 0 k_exp
exrow
else
if ft 0 k_call
callrow
else
if not ft 0 k_unit
die e_row 1
end
end
end
end
end
end
if ne ns 1
die e_son 1
end
if eq get nv 3 0
die e_noexp 1
end
for k ulong get nv 4 bound 9223372036854775807
b = mul k 16
if eq exfind get cl b get cl add b 1 get nv 3
die e_ncall 1
end
end
end
note ---- dynstr
fn dsgrow n ulong to void
if gt n len ds
r = enlarge ds add n 4096
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
end
end
note append ib[a, a+n) and a zero; its offset
fn dsib a ulong n ulong to ulong
s = get nv 2
dsgrow add add s n 1
for j ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
put ds add s j get ib add a j
end
put ds add s n 0
put nv 2 add add s n 1
ret s
end
fn dstx t view uchar * to ulong
s = get nv 2
dsgrow add add s len t 1
for j ulong len t bound 4096
put ds add s j get t j
end
put ds add s len t 0
put nv 2 add add s len t 1
ret s
end
fn dsinit to void
dsgrow 1
put ds 0 0
put nv 2 1
end
note SysV ELF hash of the dynstr string at o
fn ehash o ulong to ulong
h = ulong 0
p = o
while ne get ds p 0 bound 9223372036854775807
h = and add shl h 4 ulong get ds p 4294967295
g = and h 4026531840
if ne g 0
h = xor h shr g 24
end
h = and h not g
p = add p 1
end
ret h
end
note the dynstr offset of symbol k + 1 (library: ex 4, probe: cd)
fn symname k ulong lib bool to ulong
if lib
ret get ex add mul k 8 4
end
ret get cd k
end
note .hash at off for n symbols after the null one: n buckets, n + 1 chain entries
fn nbk n ulong to ulong
if eq n 0
ret 1
end
ret n
end
fn wrhash off ulong n ulong lib bool to void
nb = nbk n
w32 off nb
w32 add off 4 add n 1
cb = add off 8
ch = add cb mul nb 4
for k ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
s = add k 1
bo = add cb mul rem ehash symname k lib nb 4
w32 add ch mul s 4 r32 bo
w32 bo s
end
end
note copy ds to eb at off
fn wrstr off ulong to void
for j ulong get nv 2 bound 9223372036854775807
put eb add off j get ds j
end
end
fn wrbytes off ulong t view uchar * to void
for j ulong len t bound 4096
c = get t j
if eq c 32
c = 0
end
put eb add off j c
end
end
note ELF64 header: type, entry, program headers, section header offset, sections
fn wrehdr ty ulong entry ulong nph ulong shoff ulong nsh ulong to void
w32 0 1179403647
w8 4 2
w8 5 1
w8 6 1
w16 16 ty
w16 18 183
w32 20 1
w64 24 entry
w64 32 64
w64 40 shoff
w16 52 64
w16 54 56
w16 56 nph
if ne nsh 0
w16 58 64
w16 60 nsh
w16 62 sub nsh 1
end
end
note program header i; a PT_LOAD is aligned to 64 KiB, anything else to 8
fn wrph i ulong ty ulong fg ulong off ulong va ulong sz ulong to void
o = add 64 mul i 56
w32 o ty
w32 add o 4 fg
w64 add o 8 off
w64 add o 16 va
w64 add o 24 va
w64 add o 32 sz
w64 add o 40 sz
if eq ty 1
w64 add o 48 65536
else
w64 add o 48 8
end
end
note section header i (address = offset + nv 16 when allocated)
fn wrsh i ulong nm ulong ty ulong fg ulong off ulong sz ulong to void
o = add get nv 15 mul i 64
w32 o nm
w32 add o 4 ty
w64 add o 8 fg
if ne and fg 2 0
w64 add o 16 add off get nv 16
end
w64 add o 24 off
w64 add o 32 sz
end
fn wrshl i ulong lk ulong inf ulong al ulong es ulong to void
o = add get nv 15 mul i 64
w32 add o 40 lk
w32 add o 44 inf
w64 add o 48 al
w64 add o 56 es
end
fn dyn o ulong tag ulong v ulong to ulong
w64 o tag
w64 add o 8 v
ret add o 16
end
note a B or BL (op) at offset p to offset t, both in the same address space
fn wrb p ulong t ulong op ulong to void
d = sub t p
if and ge d 134217728 lt d sub ulong 0 134217728
die e_reach 1
end
w32 p or op and shr d 2 67108863
end
note ADR rd at p to t
fn wradr p ulong t ulong rd ulong to void
d = sub t p
if and ge d 1048576 lt d sub ulong 0 1048576
die e_reach 1
end
w32 p or or 268435456 rd or shl and d 3 29 shl and shr d 2 524287 5
end
note LDR X16 (literal) at p from t
fn wrldr p ulong t ulong to void
d = sub t p
if and ge d 1048576 lt d sub ulong 0 1048576
die e_reach 1
end
w32 p or 1476395024 shl and shr d 2 524287 5
end
note MOVZ (k 0) or MOVK (k 1..3, shift 16k) of the 16 bits v into rd
fn wrmov p ulong k ulong v ulong rd ulong to void
op = ulong 3531603968
if ne k 0
op = or 4068474880 shl k 21
end
w32 p or or op rd shl and v 65535 5
end
note ---- the object
fn objparse to void
b = get nv 0
e = get nv 1
if lt sub e b 176
die e_obj 1
end
for j ulong 8
if ne get ib add b j get k_obj j
die e_obj 1
end
end
if or ne oq 8 1 or ne oq 16 1 ne oq 32 176
die e_obj 1
end
c = oq 40
if or gt c sub e b lt c 176
die e_obj 1
end
if ne and c 3 0
die e_obj 1
end
put nv 8 c
nf = oq 48
nc = oq 56
put nv 7 nf
r = enlarge fr mul add nf 1 8
if lt r 0
die e_mem 3
end
o = c
for i ulong nf bound 9223372036854775807
o = frec i o
end
o = add o mul nc 32
if ne o sub e b
die e_obj 1
end
end
note function record i at object offset o into fr; the next record's offset
fn frec i ulong o ulong to ulong
b = get nv 0
f = mul i 8
put fr f oq o
put fr add f 1 oq add o 8
put fr add f 2 oq add o 16
np = oq add o 24
put fr add f 3 np
nl = oq add o 40
if gt nl 63
die e_obj 1
end
put fr add f 5 add b add o 48
put fr add f 6 nl
n = al8 add add o 48 nl
put fr add f 4 add b n
n = add n mul np 40
if gt n sub get nv 1 b
die e_obj 1
end
if eq get fr f 2
die e_imp 1
end
ret n
end
note the u32 of ib at o
fn ib32 o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for j ulong 4
v = or v shl ulong get ib add o j mul j 8
end
ret v
end
note no load of a runtime entry other than [x7, #16]: LDR (immediate, 64-bit) with Rn = x7
fn rtscan to void
b = add get nv 0 176
n = div sub get nv 8 176 4
for i ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
w = ib32 add b mul i 4
if eq and w 4290773984 4181721312
if ne and shr w 10 4095 2
die e_rt 1
end
end
end
end
fn exbind k ulong to void
x = mul k 8
a = get ex x
n = get ex add x 1
for i ulong get nv 7 bound 9223372036854775807
if fnis i a n
put ex add x 3 i
ret
end
end
die e_miss 1
end
note object function i is exported under the name ib[a, a+n)
fn fnis i ulong a ulong n ulong to bool
f = mul i 8
if or ne get fr f 1 ne get fr add f 6 n
ret false
end
ret same get fr add f 5 a n
end
note the extension of a scalar of type ty in register s: UBFX/SBFX X, X, #0, #width (0 none)
fn extw ty ulong s ulong to ulong
d = or shl s 5 s
if le ty 2
ret or 3544194048 d
end
if eq ty 3
ret or 3544202240 d
end
if eq ty 4
ret or 3544218624 d
end
if eq ty 6
ret or 2470452224 d
end
if eq ty 7
ret or 2470460416 d
end
if eq ty 8
ret or 2470476800 d
end
ret 0
end
fn isflt ty ulong to bool
ret or eq ty 10 eq ty 11
end
note parameter record o: advances the slot count nv 20; the extension word (0 none)
fn pext o ulong to ulong
ty = q o
if isflt ty
die e_flt 1
end
s = get nv 20
if eq q add o 8 0
put nv 20 add s 1
ret extw ty s
end
if eq q add o 16 0
put nv 20 add s 2
else
put nv 20 add s 1
end
ret 0
end
note the extensions of export k, written from eb offset wa when wr; their count
fn exts k ulong wr bool wa ulong to ulong
f = mul get ex add mul k 8 3 8
if isflt get fr add f 2
die e_flt 1
end
put nv 20 0
put nv 21 0
pr = get fr add f 4
for j ulong get fr add f 3 bound 6
w = pext add pr mul j 40
if ne w 0
n = get nv 21
if wr
w32 add wa mul n 4 w
end
put nv 21 add n 1
end
end
if gt get nv 20 6
die e_slot 1
end
ret get nv 21
end
note STP or LDP (op) of registers r and r + 1 at [sp, #8 * im]
fn pw op ulong r ulong im ulong to ulong
a = or shl im 15 shl add r 1 10
ret or or op a or 992 r
end
note the register save area at sp + 32: STP (LDP when back) of x19..x30 and d8..d15, 10 words from p
fn saves p ulong back bool to void
xo = ulong 2835349504
vo = ulong 1828716544
if back
xo = ulong 2839543808
vo = ulong 1832910848
end
for i ulong 6
v = pw xo add 19 mul i 2 add 4 mul i 2
w32 add p mul i 4 v
end
for i ulong 4
v = pw vo add 8 mul i 2 add 16 mul i 2
w32 add p mul add i 6 4 v
end
end
note ---- the library
note export k's wrapper: tx is the trap entry (the shared return follows it at tx + 8), cb the object's code
fn wrwrap k ulong tx ulong cb ulong to void
b = mul k 8
p = get ex add b 5
w32 p 3506635775
saves add p 4 false
wradr add p 44 tx 16
w32 add p 48 4177529840
t = get ex add b 2
wrmov add p 52 0 t 16
wrmov add p 56 1 shr t 16 16
w32 add p 60 4177530864
n = exts k true add p 64
a = add add p 64 mul n 4
w32 a 2432697319
f = mul get ex add b 3 8
wrb add a 4 add cb sub get fr add f 1 176 2483027968
wrb add a 8 add tx 8 335544320
end
note the library layout in ly: 0 .hash, 1 its bytes, 2 .dynsym, 3 .dynstr, 4 .text (the trap entry), 5 the
note object's code, 6 the end of the RX segment, 7 .dynamic (file offset), 8 .dynamic address, 9 .shstrtab,
note 10 the section headers, 11 symbols
fn liblay to void
nx = get nv 3
dsinit
put nv 13 dsib get nv 5 get nv 6
for k ulong nx bound 9223372036854775807
b = mul k 8
put ex add b 4 dsib get ex b get ex add b 1
exbind k
put ex add b 7 exts k false 0
put ex add b 6 mul add 19 get ex add b 7 4
end
rtscan
ns = add nx 1
put ly 11 ns
put ly 0 288
put ly 1 mul add nbk nx add ns 2 4
put ly 2 al8 add get ly 0 get ly 1
put ly 3 add get ly 2 mul ns 24
put ly 4 al16 add get ly 3 get nv 2
note .text: the trap entry and the shared return (14 words), the wrappers, then the object's code
wo = add get ly 4 56
for k ulong nx bound 9223372036854775807
b = mul k 8
put ex add b 5 wo
wo = add wo get ex add b 6
end
put ly 5 wo
put ly 6 add wo sub get nv 8 176
put ly 7 al16 get ly 6
put ly 8 add get ly 7 65536
put ly 9 add get ly 7 112
put ly 10 al8 add get ly 9 len t_shs
put nv 15 get ly 10
end
fn libsyms to void
wrhash get ly 0 get nv 3 true
