note ---- the probe executable (ET_EXEC at 4 MiB)
note bytes of call k's code
fn callsz k ulong to ulong
b = mul k 16
n = ulong 0
for j ulong get cl add b 3 bound 6
if eq get cl add add b 10 j 1
n = add n 1
else
n = add n 4
end
end
ret mul add n 8 4
end
note the probe layout in ly: 0 .hash, 1 its bytes, 2 .dynsym, 3 .dynstr, 4 the relocations, 5 the exit block
note (code), 6 the end of the RX segment, 7 the RW segment's file offset, 8 its address minus the base, 9 the
note file's length; the base address is 4 MiB; RW holds .dynamic (192 bytes), the GOT, then the 4096-byte buf
const PBASE ulong 4194304
note the arguments of call k from offset p; the next offset
fn wrargs k ulong p ulong to ulong
b = mul k 16
bf = add add get ly 8 192 mul get nv 4 8
for j ulong get cl add b 3 bound 6
if eq get cl add add b 10 j 1
wradr p bf j
p = add p 4
else
v = get cl add add b 4 j
for h ulong 4
u = shr v mul h 16
wrmov add p mul h 4 h u j
end
p = add p 16
end
end
ret p
end
